{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"我先把实现思路定为：用一个固定的钥匙基形（3x3 5 像素，具有明确的两格缺口侧）和可逆的方向/旋转匹配；`main` 做“按色配对→识别框体与缺口→识别钥匙朝向→旋转并平移到缺口”的确切变换；`generate_input` 用随机参数生成多个配对、随机尺寸、颜色、朝向，并控制“是否需要再旋转”分支均衡。接下来先写目标文件并运行你给的自检。"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pprint import pprint\nbase_right={(0,1),(1,1),(1,2),(2,1),(2,2)}\n\ndef rot90(coords):\n    h=3; w=3\n    return {(c, h-1-r) for r,c in coords}, w, h\n\ndef normalize(coords):\n    rs=[r for r,_ in coords]; cs=[c for _,c in coords]\n    return {(r-min(rs), c-min(cs)) for r,c in coords}\n\ndef rotate_k(coords,k):\n    h=w=3\n    cur=set(coords)\n    for _ in range(k%4):\n        cur={(c, h-1-r) for r,c in cur}\n        h,w = w,h\n    return normalize(cur)\n\nfor k,name in enumerate(['RIGHT','DOWN','LEFT','UP']):\n    c=rotate_k(base_right,k)\n    print(name,c)\n    # print grid\n    h=max(r for r,_ in c)+1\n    w=max(c0 for _,c0 in c)+1\n    g=[['.' for _ in range(w)] for __ in range(h)]\n    for r,cc in c:g[r][cc]='#'\n    print('\\\\n'.join(''.join(row) for row in g))\n    # arm cells on side with max/min coord count2\n    if name=='RIGHT': side_cells=[(r,c0) for r,c0 in c if c0==max(cc for _,cc in c)]\n    if name=='LEFT': side_cells=[(r,c0) for r,c0 in c if c0==min(cc for _,cc in c)]\n    if name=='UP': side_cells=[(r,c0) for r,c0 in c if r==min(rr for rr,_ in c)]\n    if name=='DOWN': side_cells=[(r,c0) for r,c0 in c if r==max(rr for rr,_ in c)]\n    print('arm cells',sorted(side_cells))\n    print()\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pprint import pprint\nbase_right={(0,1),(1,1),(1,2),(2,1),(2,2)}\n\ndef rot90(coords):\n    h=3; w=3\n    return {(c, h-1-r) for r,c in coords}, w, h\n\ndef normalize(coords):\n    rs=[r for r,_ in coords]; cs=[c for _,c in coords]\n    return {(r-min(rs), c-min(cs)) for r,c in coords}\n\ndef rotate_k(coords,k):\n    h=w=3\n    cur=set(coords)\n    for _ in range(k%4):\n        cur={(c, h-1-r) for r,c in cur}\n        h,w = w,h\n    return normalize(cur)\n\nfor k,name in enumerate(['RIGHT','DOWN','LEFT','UP']):\n    c=rotate_k(base_right,k)\n    print(name,c)\n    # print grid\n    h=max(r for r,_ in c)+1\n    w=max(c0 for _,c0 in c)+1\n    g=[['.' for _ in range(w)] for __ in range(h)]\n    for r,cc in c:g[r][cc]='#'\n    print('\\\\n'.join(''.join(row) for row in g))\n    # arm cells on side with max/min coord count2\n    if name=='RIGHT': side_cells=[(r,c0) for r,c0 in c if c0==max(cc for _,cc in c)]\n    if name=='LEFT': side_cells=[(r,c0) for r,c0 in c if c0==min(cc for _,cc in c)]\n    if name=='UP': side_cells=[(r,c0) for r,c0 in c if r==min(rr for rr,_ in c)]\n    if name=='DOWN': side_cells=[(r,c0) for r,c0 in c if r==max(rr for rr,_ in c)]\n    print('arm cells',sorted(side_cells))\n    print()\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"RIGHT {(2, 1), (0, 0), (1, 1), (2, 0), (1, 0)}\n#.\n##\n##\narm cells [(1, 1), (2, 1)]\n\nDOWN {(0, 1), (0, 0), (1, 1), (0, 2), (1, 0)}\n###\n##.\narm cells [(1, 0), (1, 1)]\n\nLEFT {(0, 1), (2, 1), (0, 0), (1, 1), (1, 0)}\n##\n##\n.#\narm cells [(0, 0), (1, 0)]\n\nUP {(0, 1), (1, 2), (1, 1), (0, 2), (1, 0)}\n.##\n###\narm cells [(0, 1), (0, 2)]\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"正在开始写入目标文件。先完成单文件实现（`main` + `generate_input` + 随机器与连通块工具），然后直接按你的自检脚本跑 100 次生成-求值。"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"mkdir -p /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval_new/seed202524619/2 && cat > /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval_new/seed202524619/2/2.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"将钥匙按同色容器与缺口方向完成方向匹配后嵌入容器。\n\nInput structure:\n背景色为网格中出现次数最多的颜色，另外有若干种非背景颜色。\n每种非背景颜色恰好对应一个对象：一个大空心方形边框容器（边框厚度为1且某一侧缺口宽2）和一个钥匙图形对象。\n钥匙图形与其容器同色，颜色块通常为 5 像素的 L/T 风格形状，并且有可辨识朝向。\n\nRule:\n对每种颜色先分离出容器与钥匙。\n根据容器边框缺失的两格位置确定缺口方向。\n识别钥匙的当前朝向；将钥匙在 90° 倍数内旋转到与缺口方向一致后平移。\n平移时使钥匙的突出臂（两格宽）精确覆盖缺口位置，钥匙其余部分位于容器内部。\n保留容器边框，并将钥匙从原位置移除后放入目标容器。\n\nKey insight:\n按颜色建立一一配对后，关键在于从钥匙几何形状恢复方向，再按缺口方向进行旋转对齐，之后做受约束的刚体平移。\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\n\nimport numpy as np\nfrom collections import deque\nfrom typing import Dict, Iterable, List, Optional, Sequence, Set, Tuple\n\nDIRS = [(-1, 0), (0, 1), (1, 0), (0, -1)]\nUP, RIGHT, DOWN, LEFT = 0, 1, 2, 3\n\n# 5-cell key templates, normalized coordinates (min row/col = 0).\n# Each template has a two-cell arm on the corresponding direction side.\nKEY_TEMPLATES: Dict[int, Tuple[Tuple[Tuple[int, int], ...], ...]] = {\n    UP: ((0, 1), (0, 2), (1, 0), (1, 1), (1, 2)),\n    RIGHT: ((0, 0), (1, 0), (1, 1), (2, 0), (2, 1)),\n    DOWN: ((0, 0), (0, 1), (0, 2), (1, 0), (1, 1)),\n    LEFT: ((0, 0), (0, 1), (1, 0), (1, 1), (2, 1)),\n}\nKEY_TEMPLATE_SETS: Dict[int, Set[Tuple[int, int]]] = {\n    d: set(v) for d, v in KEY_TEMPLATES.items()\n}\nKEY_ARM_CELLS: Dict[int, Set[Tuple[int, int]]] = {\n    UP: {(0, 1), (0, 2)},\n    RIGHT: {(1, 1), (2, 1)},\n    DOWN: {(1, 0), (1, 1)},\n    LEFT: {(0, 0), (1, 0)},\n}\n\n\ndef _normalize_coords(coords: Iterable[Tuple[int, int]]) -> Set[Tuple[int, int]]:\n    coords = list(coords)\n    min_r = min(r for r, _ in coords)\n    min_c = min(c for _, c in coords)\n    return {(r - min_r, c - min_c) for r, c in coords}\n\n\ndef _connected_components(mask: np.ndarray) -> List[Dict[str, object]]:\n    h, w = mask.shape\n    visited = np.zeros((h, w), dtype=bool)\n    comps: List[Dict[str, object]] = []\n\n    for sr in range(h):\n        for sc in range(w):\n            if not mask[sr, sc] or visited[sr, sc]:\n                continue\n            q = deque([(sr, sc)])\n            visited[sr, sc] = True\n            cells: List[Tuple[int, int]] = []\n            min_r = min_c = 10**9\n            max_r = max_c = -1\n            while q:\n                r, c = q.popleft()\n                cells.append((r, c))\n                if r < min_r:\n                    min_r = r\n                if r > max_r:\n                    max_r = r\n                if c < min_c:\n                    min_c = c\n                if c > max_c:\n                    max_c = c\n                nr = r - 1\n                if nr >= 0 and mask[nr, c] and not visited[nr, c]:\n                    visited[nr, c] = True\n                    q.append((nr, c))\n                nr = r + 1\n                if nr < h and mask[nr, c] and not visited[nr, c]:\n                    visited[nr, c] = True\n                    q.append((nr, c))\n                nc = c - 1\n                if nc >= 0 and mask[r, nc] and not visited[r, nc]:\n                    visited[r, nc] = True\n                    q.append((r, nc))\n                nc = c + 1\n                if nc < w and mask[r, nc] and not visited[r, nc]:\n                    visited[r, nc] = True\n                    q.append((r, nc))\n\n            comps.append(\n                {\n                    \\\"coords\\\": set(cells),\n                    \\\"bbox\\\": (min_r, max_r, min_c, max_c),\n                    \\\"size\\\": len(cells),\n                }\n            )\n    return comps\n\n\ndef _frame_gap_info(comp: Dict[str, object]) -> Optional[Tuple[int, Tuple[Tuple[int, int], Tuple[int, int]]]]:\n    coords: Set[Tuple[int, int]] = comp[\\\"coords\\\"]  # type: ignore[assignment]\n    min_r, max_r, min_c, max_c = comp[\\\"bbox\\\"]  # type: ignore[misc]\n    h = max_r - min_r + 1\n    w = max_c - min_c + 1\n\n    if h < 4 or w < 4:\n        return None\n\n    # Frame must lie on the rectangle border.\n    for r, c in coords:\n        if r \"'!= min_r and r != max_r and c != min_c and c != max_c:\n            return None\n\n    expected = 2 * (h + w) - 4\n    if len(coords) != expected - 2:\n        return None\n\n    top_missing = [c for c in range(min_c, max_c + 1) if (min_r, c) not in coords]\n    bottom_missing = [c for c in range(min_c, max_c + 1) if (max_r, c) not in coords]\n    left_missing = [r for r in range(min_r, max_r + 1) if (r, min_c) not in coords]\n    right_missing = [r for r in range(min_r, max_r + 1) if (r, max_c) not in coords]\n\n    candidates: List[Tuple[int, Tuple[Tuple[int, int], Tuple[int, int]]]] = []\n\n    if (\n        len(top_missing) == 2\n        and top_missing[0] + 1 == top_missing[1]\n        and top_missing[0] >= min_c + 1\n        and top_missing[1] <= max_c - 1\n    ):\n        c0 = top_missing[0]\n        candidates.append((UP, ((min_r, c0), (min_r, c0 + 1))))\n\n    if (\n        len(bottom_missing) == 2\n        and bottom_missing[0] + 1 == bottom_missing[1]\n        and bottom_missing[0] >= min_c + 1\n        and bottom_missing[1] <= max_c - 1\n    ):\n        c0 = bottom_missing[0]\n        candidates.append((DOWN, ((max_r, c0), (max_r, c0 + 1))))\n\n    if (\n        len(left_missing) == 2\n        and left_missing[0] + 1 == left_missing[1]\n        and left_missing[0] >= min_r + 1\n        and left_missing[1] <= max_r - 1\n    ):\n        r0 = left_missing[0]\n        candidates.append((LEFT, ((r0, min_c), (r0 + 1, min_c))))\n\n    if (\n        len(right_missing) == 2\n        and right_missing[0] + 1 == right_missing[1]\n        and right_missing[0] >= min_r + 1\n        and right_missing[1] <= max_r - 1\n    ):\n        r0 = right_missing[0]\n        candidates.append((RIGHT, ((r0, max_c), (r0 + 1, max_c))))\n\n    if len(candidates) != 1:\n        return None\n\n    return candidates[0]\n\n\ndef _detect_key_dir(comp: Dict[str, object]) -> Optional[int]:\n    coords = comp[\"coords\"]  # type: ignore[assignment]\n    norm = _normalize_coords(coords)\n    for d, tpl in KEY_TEMPLATE_SETS.items():\n        if norm == tpl:\n            return d\n    return None\n\n\ndef _translate_set(coords: Set[Tuple[int, int]], dr: int, dc: int) -> Set[Tuple[int, int]]:\n    return {(r + dr, c + dc) for r, c in coords}\n\n\ndef _fits_in_frame(\n    shape: Set[Tuple[int, int]],\n    frame: Dict[str, object],\n    arm_target: Set[Tuple[int, int]],\n    gap: Tuple[Tuple[int, int], Tuple[int, int]],\n) -> Optional[Set[Tuple[int, int]]]:\n    min_r, max_r, min_c, max_c = frame[\"bbox\"]  # type: ignore[misc]\n    gap_cells = set(gap)\n    arm_sorted = sorted(arm_target)\n    gap_sorted = sorted(gap_cells)\n\n    if len(arm_sorted) != 2 or len(gap_sorted) != 2:\n        return None\n\n    dr_candidates = {gap_sorted[i][0] - arm_sorted[i][0] for i in range(2)}\n    dc_candidates = {gap_sorted[i][1] - arm_sorted[i][1] for i in range(2)}\n    if len(dr_candidates) != 1 or len(dc_candidates) != 1:\n        return None\n\n    dr = next(iter(dr_candidates))\n    dc = next(iter(dc_candidates))\n    translated = _translate_set(shape, dr, dc)\n    translated_arm = _translate_set(arm_target, dr, dc)\n\n    if translated_arm != gap_cells:\n        return None\n\n    for r, c in translated:\n        if not (min_r <= r <= max_r and min_c <= c <= max_c):\n            return None\n    return translated\n\n\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Solve ARC transformation for keyed shape insertion.\"\"\"\n    g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)\n    out = g.copy()\n\n    if g.ndim != 2 or g.size == 0:\n        return out\n\n    vals, counts = np.unique(g, return_counts=True)\n    bg = int(vals[np.argmax(counts)])\n    colors = [int(c) for c in vals if int(c) != bg]\n\n    for color in colors:\n        mask = g == color\n        comps = _connected_components(mask)\n        if len(comps) != 2:\n            continue\n\n        frame = None\n        key = None\n        for comp in comps:\n            f = _frame_gap_info(comp)\n            if f is not None:\n                frame = comp\n                break\n\n        if frame is None:\n            frame = max(comps, key=lambda x: x[\"size\"])\n            key = min(comps, key=lambda x: x[\"size\"])\n        else:\n            key = comps[0] if comps[0] is not frame else comps[1]\n\n        frame_gap = _frame_gap_info(frame)\n        if frame_gap is None:\n            continue\n        gap_dir, gap_cells = frame_gap\n\n        key_dir = _detect_key_dir(key)\n        if key_dir is None:\n            continue\n\n        target_shape = KEY_TEMPLATE_SETS[gap_dir]\n        target_arm = KEY_ARM_CELLS[gap_dir]\n\n        placed = _fits_in_frame(target_shape, frame, target_arm, gap_cells)\n        if placed is None:\n            continue\n\n        # remove original key\n        for r, c in key[\"coords\"]:\n            out[r, c] = bg\n\n        # insert rotated/matched key\n        for r, c in placed:\n            out[r, c] = color\n\n    return out\n\n\ndef _frame_cells(\n    top: int,\n    left: int,\n    h: int,\n    w: int,\n    gap_dir: int,\n    gap_start: int,\n) -> Tuple[Set[Tuple[int, int]], Tuple[Tuple[int, int], Tuple[int, int]]]:\n    cells: Set[Tuple[int, int]] = set()\n    if gap_dir == UP:\n        gap = ((top, gap_start), (top, gap_start + 1))\n    elif gap_dir == DOWN:\n        gap = ((top + h - 1, gap_start), (top + h - 1, gap_start + 1))\n    elif gap_dir == LEFT:\n        gap = ((gap_start, left), (gap_start + 1, left))\n    else:\n        gap = ((gap_start, left + w - 1), (gap_start + 1, left + w - 1))\n\n    cells.update((top, c) for c in range(left, left + w))\n    cells.update((top + h - 1, c) for c in range(left, left + w))\n    cells.update((r, left) for r in range(top, top + h))\n    cells.update((r, left + w - 1) for r in range(top, top + h))\n\n    if gap_dir == UP:\n        cells.remove((top, gap[0][1]))\n        cells.remove((top, gap[1][1]))\n    elif gap_dir == DOWN:\n        cells.remove((top + h - 1, gap[0][1]))\n        cells.remove((top + h - 1, gap[1][1]))\n    elif gap_dir == LEFT:\n        cells.remove((gap[0][0], left))\n        cells.remove((gap[1][0], left))\n    else:\n        cells.remove((gap[0][0], left + w - 1))\n        cells.remove((gap[1][0], left + w - 1))\n\n    return cells, gap\n\n\ndef _place_pair(\n    grid: np.ndarray,\n    occ: np.ndarray,\n    color: int,\n    rng: np.random.Generator,\n    require_diverse_dirs: bool,\n    key_rotation_branch: int,\n) -> bool:\n    H, W = grid.shape\n    for _ in range(250):\n        h = int(rng.integers(7, 12))\n        w = int(rng.integers(7, 12))\n\n        if h >= H - 2 or w >= W - 2:\n            continue\n\n        top = int(rng.integers(1, H - h - 1))\n        left = int(rng.integers(1, W - w - 1))\n        gap_dir = int(rng.integers(0, 4))\n\n        if gap_dir in (UP, DOWN):\n            gap_start = int(rng.integers(left + 1, left + w - 2))\n        else:\n            gap_start = int(rng.integers(top + 1, top + h - 2))\n\n        frame_cells, gap = _frame_cells(top, left, h, w, gap_dir, gap_start)\n\n        if any(occ[r, c] for r, c in frame_cells):\n            continue\n\n        need_rotate = bool(rng.integers(0, 2) == 1)\n        if key_rotation_branch == 0:\n            key_dir = gap_dir\n            need_rotate = False\n        elif key_rotation_branch == 1:\n            key_dir = rng.integers(0, 4)\n            while key_dir == gap_dir:\n                key_dir = (key_dir + 1) % 4\n        else:\n            key_dir = int(rng.integers(0, 4))\n            if need_rotate and key_dir == gap_dir:\n                key_dir = (key_dir + 1) % 4\n            if (not need_rotate) and key_dir != gap_dir:\n                need_rotate = True\n\n        shape = KEY_TEMPLATE_SETS[key_dir]\n        kH = max(r for r, _ in shape) + 1\n        kW = max(c for _, c in shape) + 1\n\n        # place key somewhere outside the frame in free space\n        candidate_limit = 300\n        # expand frame bounds by one cell to avoid accidental touching\n        e_top = max(0, top - 1)\n        e_left = max(0, left - 1)\n        e_bottom = min(H - 1, top + h)\n        e_right = min(W - 1, left + w)\n\n        for _ in range(candidate_limit):\n            kr = int(rng.integers(0, H - kH + 1))\n            kc = int(rng.integers(0, W - kW + 1))\n\n            key_cells = {(kr + r, kc + c) for r, c in shape}\n\n            if any(occ[r, c] for r, c in key_cells):\n                continue\n\n            touches_frame = (\n                not (kr + kH - 1 < e_top or kr > e_bottom or kc + kW - 1 < e_left or kc > e_right)\n            )\n            if touches_frame:\n                continue\n\n            for r, c in frame_cells:\n                grid[r, c] = color\n                occ[r, c] = True\n            for r, c in key_cells:\n                grid[r, c] = color\n                occ[r, c] = True\n\n            return True\n    return False\n\n\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n    palette = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]\n\n    for _ in range(80):\n        rng = np.random.default_rng()\n        num_pairs = int(rng.integers(1, 3))\n        H = int(rng.integers(18, 29))\n        W = int(rng.integers(18, 29))\n        if H > 30:\n            H = 30\n        if W > 30:\n            W = 30\n\n        grid = np.zeros((H, W), dtype=int)\n        occ = np.zeros((H, W), dtype=bool)\n\n        selected_colors = palette.copy()\n        selected_colors = selected_colors[:num_pairs]\n        rng.shuffle(selected_colors)\n\n        branch_flag = int(rng.integers(0, 3))\n\n        ok = True\n        for color in selected_colors:\n            if not _place_pair(\n                grid,\n                occ,\n                color,\n                rng,\n                require_diverse_dirs=True,\n                key_rotation_branch=branch_flag,\n            ):\n                ok = False\n                break\n\n        if not ok:\n            continue\n\n        # ensure all colors have exactly one frame+one key in this sample\n        for color in selected_colors:\n            comps = _connected_components(grid == color)\n            if len(comps) != 2:\n                ok = False\n                break\n        if not ok:\n            continue\n\n        return grid\n\n    # deterministic fallback\n    grid = np.zeros((22, 22), dtype=int)\n    _place_pair(\n        grid,\n        np.zeros_like(grid, dtype=bool),\n        1,\n        np.random.default_rng(0),\n        require_diverse_dirs=True,\n        key_rotation_branch=2,\n    )\n    return grid\n\nPY'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"mkdir -p /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval_new/seed202524619/2 && cat > /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval_new/seed202524619/2/2.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"将钥匙按同色容器与缺口方向完成方向匹配后嵌入容器。\n\nInput structure:\n背景色为网格中出现次数最多的颜色，另外有若干种非背景颜色。\n每种非背景颜色恰好对应一个对象：一个大空心方形边框容器（边框厚度为1且某一侧缺口宽2）和一个钥匙图形对象。\n钥匙图形与其容器同色，颜色块通常为 5 像素的 L/T 风格形状，并且有可辨识朝向。\n\nRule:\n对每种颜色先分离出容器与钥匙。\n根据容器边框缺失的两格位置确定缺口方向。\n识别钥匙的当前朝向；将钥匙在 90° 倍数内旋转到与缺口方向一致后平移。\n平移时使钥匙的突出臂（两格宽）精确覆盖缺口位置，钥匙其余部分位于容器内部。\n保留容器边框，并将钥匙从原位置移除后放入目标容器。\n\nKey insight:\n按颜色建立一一配对后，关键在于从钥匙几何形状恢复方向，再按缺口方向进行旋转对齐，之后做受约束的刚体平移。\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\n\nimport numpy as np\nfrom collections import deque\nfrom typing import Dict, Iterable, List, Optional, Sequence, Set, Tuple\n\nDIRS = [(-1, 0), (0, 1), (1, 0), (0, -1)]\nUP, RIGHT, DOWN, LEFT = 0, 1, 2, 3\n\n# 5-cell key templates, normalized coordinates (min row/col = 0).\n# Each template has a two-cell arm on the corresponding direction side.\nKEY_TEMPLATES: Dict[int, Tuple[Tuple[Tuple[int, int], ...], ...]] = {\n    UP: ((0, 1), (0, 2), (1, 0), (1, 1), (1, 2)),\n    RIGHT: ((0, 0), (1, 0), (1, 1), (2, 0), (2, 1)),\n    DOWN: ((0, 0), (0, 1), (0, 2), (1, 0), (1, 1)),\n    LEFT: ((0, 0), (0, 1), (1, 0), (1, 1), (2, 1)),\n}\nKEY_TEMPLATE_SETS: Dict[int, Set[Tuple[int, int]]] = {\n    d: set(v) for d, v in KEY_TEMPLATES.items()\n}\nKEY_ARM_CELLS: Dict[int, Set[Tuple[int, int]]] = {\n    UP: {(0, 1), (0, 2)},\n    RIGHT: {(1, 1), (2, 1)},\n    DOWN: {(1, 0), (1, 1)},\n    LEFT: {(0, 0), (1, 0)},\n}\n\n\ndef _normalize_coords(coords: Iterable[Tuple[int, int]]) -> Set[Tuple[int, int]]:\n    coords = list(coords)\n    min_r = min(r for r, _ in coords)\n    min_c = min(c for _, c in coords)\n    return {(r - min_r, c - min_c) for r, c in coords}\n\n\ndef _connected_components(mask: np.ndarray) -> List[Dict[str, object]]:\n    h, w = mask.shape\n    visited = np.zeros((h, w), dtype=bool)\n    comps: List[Dict[str, object]] = []\n\n    for sr in range(h):\n        for sc in range(w):\n            if not mask[sr, sc] or visited[sr, sc]:\n                continue\n            q = deque([(sr, sc)])\n            visited[sr, sc] = True\n            cells: List[Tuple[int, int]] = []\n            min_r = min_c = 10**9\n            max_r = max_c = -1\n            while q:\n                r, c = q.popleft()\n                cells.append((r, c))\n                if r < min_r:\n                    min_r = r\n                if r > max_r:\n                    max_r = r\n                if c < min_c:\n                    min_c = c\n                if c > max_c:\n                    max_c = c\n                nr = r - 1\n                if nr >= 0 and mask[nr, c] and not visited[nr, c]:\n                    visited[nr, c] = True\n                    q.append((nr, c))\n                nr = r + 1\n                if nr < h and mask[nr, c] and not visited[nr, c]:\n                    visited[nr, c] = True\n                    q.append((nr, c))\n                nc = c - 1\n                if nc >= 0 and mask[r, nc] and not visited[r, nc]:\n                    visited[r, nc] = True\n                    q.append((r, nc))\n                nc = c + 1\n                if nc < w and mask[r, nc] and not visited[r, nc]:\n                    visited[r, nc] = True\n                    q.append((r, nc))\n\n            comps.append(\n                {\n                    \\\"coords\\\": set(cells),\n                    \\\"bbox\\\": (min_r, max_r, min_c, max_c),\n                    \\\"size\\\": len(cells),\n                }\n            )\n    return comps\n\n\ndef _frame_gap_info(comp: Dict[str, object]) -> Optional[Tuple[int, Tuple[Tuple[int, int], Tuple[int, int]]]]:\n    coords: Set[Tuple[int, int]] = comp[\\\"coords\\\"]  # type: ignore[assignment]\n    min_r, max_r, min_c, max_c = comp[\\\"bbox\\\"]  # type: ignore[misc]\n    h = max_r - min_r + 1\n    w = max_c - min_c + 1\n\n    if h < 4 or w < 4:\n        return None\n\n    # Frame must lie on the rectangle border.\n    for r, c in coords:\n        if r \"'!= min_r and r != max_r and c != min_c and c != max_c:\n            return None\n\n    expected = 2 * (h + w) - 4\n    if len(coords) != expected - 2:\n        return None\n\n    top_missing = [c for c in range(min_c, max_c + 1) if (min_r, c) not in coords]\n    bottom_missing = [c for c in range(min_c, max_c + 1) if (max_r, c) not in coords]\n    left_missing = [r for r in range(min_r, max_r + 1) if (r, min_c) not in coords]\n    right_missing = [r for r in range(min_r, max_r + 1) if (r, max_c) not in coords]\n\n    candidates: List[Tuple[int, Tuple[Tuple[int, int], Tuple[int, int]]]] = []\n\n    if (\n        len(top_missing) == 2\n        and top_missing[0] + 1 == top_missing[1]\n        and top_missing[0] >= min_c + 1\n        and top_missing[1] <= max_c - 1\n    ):\n        c0 = top_missing[0]\n        candidates.append((UP, ((min_r, c0), (min_r, c0 + 1))))\n\n    if (\n        len(bottom_missing) == 2\n        and bottom_missing[0] + 1 == bottom_missing[1]\n        and bottom_missing[0] >= min_c + 1\n        and bottom_missing[1] <= max_c - 1\n    ):\n        c0 = bottom_missing[0]\n        candidates.append((DOWN, ((max_r, c0), (max_r, c0 + 1))))\n\n    if (\n        len(left_missing) == 2\n        and left_missing[0] + 1 == left_missing[1]\n        and left_missing[0] >= min_r + 1\n        and left_missing[1] <= max_r - 1\n    ):\n        r0 = left_missing[0]\n        candidates.append((LEFT, ((r0, min_c), (r0 + 1, min_c))))\n\n    if (\n        len(right_missing) == 2\n        and right_missing[0] + 1 == right_missing[1]\n        and right_missing[0] >= min_r + 1\n        and right_missing[1] <= max_r - 1\n    ):\n        r0 = right_missing[0]\n        candidates.append((RIGHT, ((r0, max_c), (r0 + 1, max_c))))\n\n    if len(candidates) != 1:\n        return None\n\n    return candidates[0]\n\n\ndef _detect_key_dir(comp: Dict[str, object]) -> Optional[int]:\n    coords = comp[\"coords\"]  # type: ignore[assignment]\n    norm = _normalize_coords(coords)\n    for d, tpl in KEY_TEMPLATE_SETS.items():\n        if norm == tpl:\n            return d\n    return None\n\n\ndef _translate_set(coords: Set[Tuple[int, int]], dr: int, dc: int) -> Set[Tuple[int, int]]:\n    return {(r + dr, c + dc) for r, c in coords}\n\n\ndef _fits_in_frame(\n    shape: Set[Tuple[int, int]],\n    frame: Dict[str, object],\n    arm_target: Set[Tuple[int, int]],\n    gap: Tuple[Tuple[int, int], Tuple[int, int]],\n) -> Optional[Set[Tuple[int, int]]]:\n    min_r, max_r, min_c, max_c = frame[\"bbox\"]  # type: ignore[misc]\n    gap_cells = set(gap)\n    arm_sorted = sorted(arm_target)\n    gap_sorted = sorted(gap_cells)\n\n    if len(arm_sorted) != 2 or len(gap_sorted) != 2:\n        return None\n\n    dr_candidates = {gap_sorted[i][0] - arm_sorted[i][0] for i in range(2)}\n    dc_candidates = {gap_sorted[i][1] - arm_sorted[i][1] for i in range(2)}\n    if len(dr_candidates) != 1 or len(dc_candidates) != 1:\n        return None\n\n    dr = next(iter(dr_candidates))\n    dc = next(iter(dc_candidates))\n    translated = _translate_set(shape, dr, dc)\n    translated_arm = _translate_set(arm_target, dr, dc)\n\n    if translated_arm != gap_cells:\n        return None\n\n    for r, c in translated:\n        if not (min_r <= r <= max_r and min_c <= c <= max_c):\n            return None\n    return translated\n\n\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Solve ARC transformation for keyed shape insertion.\"\"\"\n    g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)\n    out = g.copy()\n\n    if g.ndim != 2 or g.size == 0:\n        return out\n\n    vals, counts = np.unique(g, return_counts=True)\n    bg = int(vals[np.argmax(counts)])\n    colors = [int(c) for c in vals if int(c) != bg]\n\n    for color in colors:\n        mask = g == color\n        comps = _connected_components(mask)\n        if len(comps) != 2:\n            continue\n\n        frame = None\n        key = None\n        for comp in comps:\n            f = _frame_gap_info(comp)\n            if f is not None:\n                frame = comp\n                break\n\n        if frame is None:\n            frame = max(comps, key=lambda x: x[\"size\"])\n            key = min(comps, key=lambda x: x[\"size\"])\n        else:\n            key = comps[0] if comps[0] is not frame else comps[1]\n\n        frame_gap = _frame_gap_info(frame)\n        if frame_gap is None:\n            continue\n        gap_dir, gap_cells = frame_gap\n\n        key_dir = _detect_key_dir(key)\n        if key_dir is None:\n            continue\n\n        target_shape = KEY_TEMPLATE_SETS[gap_dir]\n        target_arm = KEY_ARM_CELLS[gap_dir]\n\n        placed = _fits_in_frame(target_shape, frame, target_arm, gap_cells)\n        if placed is None:\n            continue\n\n        # remove original key\n        for r, c in key[\"coords\"]:\n            out[r, c] = bg\n\n        # insert rotated/matched key\n        for r, c in placed:\n            out[r, c] = color\n\n    return out\n\n\ndef _frame_cells(\n    top: int,\n    left: int,\n    h: int,\n    w: int,\n    gap_dir: int,\n    gap_start: int,\n) -> Tuple[Set[Tuple[int, int]], Tuple[Tuple[int, int], Tuple[int, int]]]:\n    cells: Set[Tuple[int, int]] = set()\n    if gap_dir == UP:\n        gap = ((top, gap_start), (top, gap_start + 1))\n    elif gap_dir == DOWN:\n        gap = ((top + h - 1, gap_start), (top + h - 1, gap_start + 1))\n    elif gap_dir == LEFT:\n        gap = ((gap_start, left), (gap_start + 1, left))\n    else:\n        gap = ((gap_start, left + w - 1), (gap_start + 1, left + w - 1))\n\n    cells.update((top, c) for c in range(left, left + w))\n    cells.update((top + h - 1, c) for c in range(left, left + w))\n    cells.update((r, left) for r in range(top, top + h))\n    cells.update((r, left + w - 1) for r in range(top, top + h))\n\n    if gap_dir == UP:\n        cells.remove((top, gap[0][1]))\n        cells.remove((top, gap[1][1]))\n    elif gap_dir == DOWN:\n        cells.remove((top + h - 1, gap[0][1]))\n        cells.remove((top + h - 1, gap[1][1]))\n    elif gap_dir == LEFT:\n        cells.remove((gap[0][0], left))\n        cells.remove((gap[1][0], left))\n    else:\n        cells.remove((gap[0][0], left + w - 1))\n        cells.remove((gap[1][0], left + w - 1))\n\n    return cells, gap\n\n\ndef _place_pair(\n    grid: np.ndarray,\n    occ: np.ndarray,\n    color: int,\n    rng: np.random.Generator,\n    require_diverse_dirs: bool,\n    key_rotation_branch: int,\n) -> bool:\n    H, W = grid.shape\n    for _ in range(250):\n        h = int(rng.integers(7, 12))\n        w = int(rng.integers(7, 12))\n\n        if h >= H - 2 or w >= W - 2:\n            continue\n\n        top = int(rng.integers(1, H - h - 1))\n        left = int(rng.integers(1, W - w - 1))\n        gap_dir = int(rng.integers(0, 4))\n\n        if gap_dir in (UP, DOWN):\n            gap_start = int(rng.integers(left + 1, left + w - 2))\n        else:\n            gap_start = int(rng.integers(top + 1, top + h - 2))\n\n        frame_cells, gap = _frame_cells(top, left, h, w, gap_dir, gap_start)\n\n        if any(occ[r, c] for r, c in frame_cells):\n            continue\n\n        need_rotate = bool(rng.integers(0, 2) == 1)\n        if key_rotation_branch == 0:\n            key_dir = gap_dir\n            need_rotate = False\n        elif key_rotation_branch == 1:\n            key_dir = rng.integers(0, 4)\n            while key_dir == gap_dir:\n                key_dir = (key_dir + 1) % 4\n        else:\n            key_dir = int(rng.integers(0, 4))\n            if need_rotate and key_dir == gap_dir:\n                key_dir = (key_dir + 1) % 4\n            if (not need_rotate) and key_dir != gap_dir:\n                need_rotate = True\n\n        shape = KEY_TEMPLATE_SETS[key_dir]\n        kH = max(r for r, _ in shape) + 1\n        kW = max(c for _, c in shape) + 1\n\n        # place key somewhere outside the frame in free space\n        candidate_limit = 300\n        # expand frame bounds by one cell to avoid accidental touching\n        e_top = max(0, top - 1)\n        e_left = max(0, left - 1)\n        e_bottom = min(H - 1, top + h)\n        e_right = min(W - 1, left + w)\n\n        for _ in range(candidate_limit):\n            kr = int(rng.integers(0, H - kH + 1))\n            kc = int(rng.integers(0, W - kW + 1))\n\n            key_cells = {(kr + r, kc + c) for r, c in shape}\n\n            if any(occ[r, c] for r, c in key_cells):\n                continue\n\n            touches_frame = (\n                not (kr + kH - 1 < e_top or kr > e_bottom or kc + kW - 1 < e_left or kc > e_right)\n            )\n            if touches_frame:\n                continue\n\n            for r, c in frame_cells:\n                grid[r, c] = color\n                occ[r, c] = True\n            for r, c in key_cells:\n                grid[r, c] = color\n                occ[r, c] = True\n\n            return True\n    return False\n\n\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n    palette = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]\n\n    for _ in range(80):\n        rng = np.random.default_rng()\n        num_pairs = int(rng.integers(1, 3))\n        H = int(rng.integers(18, 29))\n        W = int(rng.integers(18, 29))\n        if H > 30:\n            H = 30\n        if W > 30:\n            W = 30\n\n        grid = np.zeros((H, W), dtype=int)\n        occ = np.zeros((H, W), dtype=bool)\n\n        selected_colors = palette.copy()\n        selected_colors = selected_colors[:num_pairs]\n        rng.shuffle(selected_colors)\n\n        branch_flag = int(rng.integers(0, 3))\n\n        ok = True\n        for color in selected_colors:\n            if not _place_pair(\n                grid,\n                occ,\n                color,\n                rng,\n                require_diverse_dirs=True,\n                key_rotation_branch=branch_flag,\n            ):\n                ok = False\n                break\n\n        if not ok:\n            continue\n\n        # ensure all colors have exactly one frame+one key in this sample\n        for color in selected_colors:\n            comps = _connected_components(grid == color)\n            if len(comps) != 2:\n                ok = False\n                break\n        if not ok:\n            continue\n\n        return grid\n\n    # deterministic fallback\n    grid = np.zeros((22, 22), dtype=int)\n    _place_pair(\n        grid,\n        np.zeros_like(grid, dtype=bool),\n        1,\n        np.random.default_rng(0),\n        require_diverse_dirs=True,\n        key_rotation_branch=2,\n    )\n    return grid\n\nPY'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
